        'Time is treasure. What you spend your time on reveals what you actually value — not what you say you value, but what your calendar and your phone screen time prove you value. For Quality Time people, the absence of your focused attention communicates absence of love, regardless of how much you do for them or say to them.',
        'The beloved in Song of Solomon doesn\'t just coexist with the other — they invite: "Rise up, come away." Quality time thrives on intention and invitation. Planning something specifically for someone says: "I thought about you. I wanted to be with YOU specifically."',
        'Martha is doing everything right and still getting it wrong. Mary is just sitting with Jesus. He says Mary chose better. Sometimes the most loving thing you can do is not do more — it\'s stop and be fully present. The doers in our lives need to hear this most.',
        'Intentional connection happens in the margins of ordinary life — not just on special occasions. The dinner table, the car ride, the bedtime routine. The families and friendships with the deepest bonds have learned to protect these ordinary moments as sacred.',
        'Quality time doesn\'t require hours. It requires intention. Five fully-present minutes beats two hours of distracted togetherness. The quality-time person in your life is not asking for more of your clock — they are asking for more of your actual attention.',
        'When Job\'s friends arrived, they sat with him in silence for seven days. They didn\'t fix, explain, or theologize. They showed up and stayed. That is one of the most profound acts of love in all of Scripture — presence without agenda in the middle of pain.',
