    bible: { book: 'Joshua', chapter: 24, verse_range: '15', key_verse: '"Choose for yourselves this day whom you will serve." — Joshua 24:15', devotion: 'Joshua didn\'t express hope or set intentions. He made a declaration. Love going forward is not about good feelings — it is about commitments made on ordinary days when feelings are irrelevant. The commitments you make today, sustained through the days when you don\'t feel like it, are what transform relationships over years and decades.', reflection_q: 'What commitments — not goals, not intentions, but commitments — do you want to make about how you love the people in your life going forward?' },
    workout: { premade_id: 'beginner-full-body', motivational_tip: 'Write 5 specific love commitments: not "I will be better" but specific daily decisions. "I will put my phone away at dinner." "I will initiate repair within 24 hours of conflict." "I will speak one specific affirmation daily." Write them. Read them every morning for 30 days.', coach_note: 'Write your 5 love commitments somewhere permanent — your journal, a card, your phone notes. A commitment written is a commitment strengthened.' },
    nutrition: { focus: 'The 5 Love Commitments', meal_theme: 'Commitment vs. Intention', plan: 'Write exactly 5 specific love commitments — not aspirations, not intentions, but commitments. Use specific, behavioral language: "I will [specific action] [specific frequency] with [specific person or in general]." Post them somewhere visible. Read them every morning for the next 30 days. These commitments are the infrastructure of the love culture you\'ve been building for 8 weeks.', tip: 'A commitment is a decision made in advance so you don\'t have to make it again every day. The daily re-decision is exhausting and unreliable. A commitment removes the decision and replaces it with a practice.', recipe_search: 'commitment love daily practice' },
